    <s:String x:Key="HelpIntroTitle">Purpose</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="HelpIntro">NewYoutubeDownloader downloads single videos, playlists and channels from YouTube, Rutube and VK Video, and transcodes files that are already on disk.&#10;&#10;The main window has the tabs Search, Queue, Bulk download and Transcode. The title-bar buttons open the main screen, Settings, this help and the about page. The link to the source repository is shown above this text.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="HelpDownloadTitle">Search and download</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="HelpDownload">On the Search tab, paste a link to a video, a playlist or a channel. The program then shows the title, the author, the view count and the number of videos.&#10;&#10;Download opens the progress screen. Add to queue places the job in the queue and leaves the main window open. Back on the download screen returns to Search and keeps a job that has already started: the job continues on the Queue tab.&#10;&#10;The folder, format, quality and file-name pattern are set with Options.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="HelpSourcesTitle">Sources and accounts</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="HelpSources">Links to a video, a playlist or a channel are accepted from YouTube, Rutube and VK Video. Public items download without an account.&#10;&#10;Full YouTube quality and restricted videos use a saved session. Under YouTube account, sign in inside the program or import a Firefox session. Rutube offers the same two actions; closed and restricted Rutube videos download through that session. Sign out removes the saved session.&#10;&#10;The program has no separate sign-in for VK Video. It downloads the public items of that source.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="HelpPlaylistsTitle">Playlists and bulk download</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="HelpPlaylists">When Save each playlist in its own folder is on, a playlist is written to a folder that carries its title. Files are numbered in list order. At the end the program writes an .m3u playlist for sequential playback.&#10;&#10;Find other playlists collects playlists from the page. A channel playlist catalog expands into that list. Add to bulk download sends the selected rows to the queue. When nothing is selected, the whole found list is sent.&#10;&#10;On the Bulk download tab, place several links, one on each line. Text may be dropped onto the field. Download puts those links into the queue.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="HelpQueueTitle">Queue</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="HelpQueue">The Queue tab lists jobs with the title, the current file, the folder, the progress, the state, the speed and the video count. The filter keeps rows by title, folder or link. Several jobs are selected with Ctrl and Shift.&#10;&#10;The selection can be paused, resumed, moved up, moved down, moved to the top or to the bottom, or cancelled. Pause frees a download slot and stops only the current video. Cancel removes the job. The right-click menu repeats these commands and adds Open folder, Copy link and Copy path. A double-click on a job opens its folder.&#10;&#10;Ctrl+A selects every job. Delete cancels the selection. Space switches pause. Ctrl+Up and Ctrl+Down move the job in the list.&#10;&#10;The lower pane belongs to the focused job. Its file list shows the number, the title, the file name and the state. The selected files can be paused, resumed, given priority, or retried. Retry returns a failed file to the queue while that job is still running. In the file menu, Download next is the same priority command. The menu also opens the file or its folder, copies the file name, and selects every file, the failed files or the paused files. A double-click opens a finished file, and opens the job folder for any other row.&#10;&#10;On resume the program checks the files already in the folder against the whole playlist, including gaps in the middle. A finished file whose duration is close to the video duration counts as downloaded. An incomplete .part file, and a leftover .ytdl file, stay in the queue. The counter is the number of checked files out of the whole playlist.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="HelpSettingsTitle">Settings</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="HelpSettings">Dark theme and the Color list set the appearance. Save my download preferences stores the choices made in Options.&#10;&#10;Limit the number of simultaneous conversions caps how many files are converted during a download. The new limit applies after a restart. Simultaneous encodes belongs to transcoding of files that are already downloaded, and it applies at once: extra processes stop, and the freed places are taken by the next files. The same value is set in Options and on the Transcode tab.&#10;&#10;At startup the interface language follows the Windows language. A string that has no translation is shown in English. The Language list changes the language until the next launch. YouTube account and Rutube account are described under Sources and accounts.</s:String>
